note.paragraph:
Given $\mathbf{b} = \begin{bmatrix}
      b_{1} \\
       \vdots \\
      b_{m}
      \end{bmatrix}$ in $\text{ℝ}^{m}$, $\mathbf{c} = \begin{bmatrix}
      c_{1} \\
       \vdots \\
      c_{n}
      \end{bmatrix}$ in $\text{ℝ}^{n}$, and an $m \times n$ matrix $A = \begin{bmatrix}
      a_{ij}
      \end{bmatrix}$, the canonical linear programming problem is the following:

Find an $n\text{-tuple}$ $\mathbf{x} = \begin{bmatrix}
      x_{1} \\
       \vdots \\
      x_{m}
      \end{bmatrix}$ in $\text{ℝ}^{n}$ to maximize

paragraph.math:
$$\begin{matrix}
      \left\{ \begin{array}{lllllll}
      x_{1} & + & x_{2} & + & x_{3} & = & 50 \\
      x_{1} & + & {2x_{2}} & + & {4x_{3}} & = & 80 \\
       & & & & x_{3} & = & 0
      \end{array} \right. & \Rightarrow & \left\{ \begin{array}{lllll}
      x_{1} & + & x_{2} & = & 50 \\
      x_{1} & + & {2x_{2}} & = & 80
      \end{array} \right.
      \end{matrix}$$

statement.paragraph:
Let $\textbf{v} = \begin{bmatrix}
      a \\
      b
      \end{bmatrix}$ and $\textbf{x} = \begin{bmatrix}
      x_{1} \\
      x_{2}
      \end{bmatrix}$. The inequality $ax_{1} + bx_{2} \leq c$ for some real number $c$ may be written as $\textbf{v}^{T}\textbf{x} \leq c$. The set $S$ of all $\mathbf{x}$ that satisfy this inequality is called a closed half-space of $\textbf{ℝ}^{2}$. Show that $S$ is convex. [See the Hint for Exercise 18.]
